# Source business data -- the original Express exports.
# Deliberately NOT committed: 4.6 MB of raw sales records including every
# customer name. It is re-uploaded through the website, which is the whole
# point of the upload endpoint. Remove this line only if you have decided
# the repository is private and you want the raw exports version-controlled.
data/raw/

# Parsed tables. 9.5 MB, and customer_rfm.csv carries 1,483 customer names.
# Rebuilt on every upload, so nothing is lost by excluding it -- and it keeps
# personally identifying customer data out of the git host. The aggregates in
# data/app/ ARE committed: they are group-level, 156 KB, and they let the
# deployed site show real numbers before the first upload.
data/clean/

# Dashboard aggregates. These were committed so the deployed site could show
# real numbers before the first upload. Supabase now holds the full dataset,
# so that job is done -- and these files carry real revenue (kpi_monthly,
# sales_by_group_month) and per-salesperson performance. Keeping them out of
# git means no real figure is version-controlled anywhere.
#
# With no database AND no snapshot the API returns 503 "กรุณาอัปโหลดไฟล์ก่อน"
# rather than inventing numbers -- a loud failure, which is the right one.
# To restore the offline demo fallback: git add -f data/app/*.csv
data/app/*.csv
!data/app/README.md

# Same reasoning for the forecast intermediates: all generated by
# forecast_baseline.py / forecast_plan.py on every run, and
# dead_stock_risk.csv carries per-SKU total_revenue_ex_vat.
# data/reference/product_groups.csv is NOT ignored -- it is a hand-curated
# input the pipeline reads, and it holds no revenue.
data/forecast/*.csv

# Analyst scratch space: fuzzy-match suggestions and debug dumps.
data/review/
data/sample/

# Local scratch
.tmp/
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.venv/
venv/
.env
.env.local

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/settings.local.json
